# Sabai Stellar PoC — environment template (testnet only)
#
# Copy to .env and run `npm run setup-multisig` from scripts/. Anything missing
# below is generated and written back into .env for you, and only the public
# `G…` addresses are printed — a secret on stdout ends up in terminal
# scrollback and in any screen recording.
#
# To fill it in by hand instead:
#   stellar keys generate <name> --network testnet --fund
#   stellar keys show <name>      # secret (S...)
#   stellar keys address <name>   # public (G...)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployer: uploads the wasm and pays the deploy fees. Also `fee_to`, the
# account the platform's commission lands on. Holds no contract role.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEPLOYER_SECRET=S...
DEPLOYER_PUBLIC=G...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin: the 2-of-3 multisig ACCOUNT that is the admin of all five contracts.
#
# Not a contract imitating multisig — an ordinary Stellar account whose signer
# list and thresholds the network itself enforces. Everything that can issue
# shares, confiscate them, reprice the sale, withdraw funds, replace the code
# or hand the role on needs two of the three signers below.
#
# ADMIN_SECRET is the account's master key. `setup-multisig` sets its weight to
# zero, so afterwards it can authorize nothing on its own; it is kept only so
# the account can be rebuilt after a testnet reset.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADMIN_SECRET=S...
ADMIN_PUBLIC=G...
ADMIN_SIGNER_1_SECRET=S...
ADMIN_SIGNER_2_SECRET=S...
ADMIN_SIGNER_3_SECRET=S...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operator: one hot key for running the asset day to day. Halts the deployment,
# opens and closes the markets, force-cancels an order, distributes a rent
# round. It cannot move a share, change a price, withdraw anything, or promote
# itself — `npm run governance-drill` proves each of those on-chain.
#
# This is the key to connect in Freighter when opening /admin.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPERATOR_SECRET=S...
OPERATOR_PUBLIC=G...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Treasury: custody of the issuance and recipient of the sale proceeds. Needs
# its own secret, not just an address: the shares are minted here, and moving a
# tranche into the sale contract is signed by THIS key rather than the admin's.
# It is also the fixed destination of a forced revocation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TREASURY_SECRET=S...
TREASURY_PUBLIC=G...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KYC provider: the ONLY address allowed to admit, suspend or revoke investors
# (compliance-registry.register_verified / freeze / revoke). Deliberately
# separate from both the admin and the operator: the party that decides who may
# invest is not the party holding the money. In production this is the licensed
# provider's key; here it is ours, and it needs XLM to pay its own fees.
# Falls back to DEPLOYER_PUBLIC.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
KYC_PROVIDER_SECRET=S...
KYC_PROVIDER_PUBLIC=G...
